@startuml
title US44 - Weather Person Remote Access Scenario

actor "Weather Person" as WeatherPerson
boundary "TCP Client" as Client
control "TCP Server\nRemoteAccessTcpServer" as TcpServer
control "WeatherRemoteAccessController" as RemoteController
control "Weather EAPLI Controllers" as EapliControllers
database "AISafe Database" as DB
control "UDP Log Client" as UdpClient
control "Remote Accesses\nLogging Server" as LoggingServer
boundary "Browser" as Browser

WeatherPerson -> Client : Enter SERVICE|US44
Client -> TcpServer : SERVICE|US44
TcpServer -> RemoteController : create US44 handler
TcpServer --> Client : service selected

WeatherPerson -> Client : LOGIN|username|password
Client -> TcpServer : LOGIN|username|password
TcpServer -> RemoteController : handle LOGIN
RemoteController --> TcpServer : OK or ERROR
TcpServer -> UdpClient : log LOGIN_SUCCESS/LOGIN_FAILED
UdpClient -> LoggingServer : UDP event
TcpServer --> Client : response

WeatherPerson -> Client : Weather command
Client -> TcpServer : CONSULT/REGISTER/IMPORT command
TcpServer -> RemoteController : handle command
RemoteController -> EapliControllers : delegate weather use case
EapliControllers -> DB : repository access
DB --> EapliControllers : domain data
EapliControllers --> RemoteController : result
RemoteController --> TcpServer : OK/DATA/ERROR
TcpServer --> Client : response

WeatherPerson -> Client : LOGOUT
Client -> TcpServer : LOGOUT
TcpServer -> RemoteController : handle LOGOUT
TcpServer -> UdpClient : log LOGOUT
UdpClient -> LoggingServer : UDP event
TcpServer --> Client : session closed

Browser -> LoggingServer : GET /events or /active-users
LoggingServer --> Browser : HTML/AJAX log view

@enduml
